facts.claim:
muse.ai is operated by Meta today. Observed on 2026-10-06:
- the nameservers are a/b/c/d.ns.facebook.com;
- the security header (CSP) allows *.meta.ai and *.facebook.com;
- muse.ai redirects to auth.muse.ai/aymh, which redirects to facebook.com/aymh (Meta login);
- muse.ai/platform shows a '(c) 2026 Meta' footer.

Meta's connector guidelines require:
- business verification, a test account and three review stages (risk assessment, tool review, end-to-end QA);
- that a connector "Add value beyond the browser";
- tool permissions are Read or Write: "Ask on first use", with "Always allow" possible except for sensitive writes.
Approved connectors appear in Settings > Connectors and Muse can discover them.

The Jev Minecraft harness (rmalde/minecraft-agent):
- uses Mineflayer with structured game state, not screenshots;
- has bounded actions (travel, mine one block, collect, craft, open chest, eat, sleep, combat);
- calls models through OpenAI-compatible APIs via OpenRouter (planner gpt-6-astra, picker typesafe/jev-1.13);
- records video with Prismarine Viewer.

Meta Model API:
- base URL https://api.meta.ai/v1, compatible with the OpenAI and Anthropic SDKs;
- Muse Spark has a 1,048,576-token context;
- public preview for US developers with $20 in free credits;
- $1.25 per million input tokens, $4.25 per million output (Spark 1.1 pricing).
